{title: He Cares for You}
{subtitle: 1 Peter 5:6–7}
{key: C}
{tempo: 81}
{time: 6/8}

{comment: Intro}
| [C] | [C] | [C] | [Am] |
| [Am] | [Fmaj7] | [Fmaj7] | [C] |
| [G] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]I been [C]carrying my troubles like a sack of stones [Am]
Carry[Fmaj7]ing them down the highway, carrying them home
Carried them to bed at night and woke up with them [Am]too
Lord, I'm [Fmaj7]tired of carrying, don't know what to [C]do
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Casting [Am]all your [G]anxiety on [Fmaj7]him
Because he cares for [C]you
Casting [Am]all your [G]anxiety on [Fmaj7]him
Because he cares for [C]you
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Old fisherman Peter learned it hard and [Am]slow
He [Fmaj7]wrote it in a letter so the rest of [C]us would know
Humble yourselves under God's mighty [Am]hand
So that [Fmaj7]he may lift you up in due [C]time
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Casting [Am]all your [G]anxiety on [Fmaj7]him
Because he cares for [C]you
Casting [Am]all your anx[G]iety on [Fmaj7]him
Because he cares for [C]you
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Fmaj7]Set it down, [G]set it down
[Am]Lay your heavy [G6]burden on the ground
[Fmaj7]Set it down, set it [C]down
He cares for you [Am]
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Because he cares for [C]you [Am]
Because he cares for [C]you
{end_of_verse}
